WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.550
Oldham, 1978.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:07.040
Louise Brown is born, the
first baby conceived by I V F,

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.490
in a laboratory.

4
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.950
Today, I V F often makes more
embryos than are transferred.

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.680
The spare ones may be frozen,
donated, or allowed to perish.

6
00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.710
An ancient psalm calls children
a heritage of the LORD.

7
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.560
So is a child a gift or a right?

8
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:28.310
And who decides what happens
to embryos made in a lab?

9
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.160
In this mission, you'll see what different
traditions say an embryo in a dish

10
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.290
is owed.

11
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.550
Then you'll weigh up surrogacy, and who
the law counts as a child's mother at

12
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.750
birth.

13
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.000
Your mission: work out whether
a child is a gift or a right,

14
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.090
and who decides about embryos.
